Gardenfell is licensed in two parts, because two licences apply.

The engine and the command line, everything under crates/ (the gardenfell-* library
crates, gardenfell-session among them, gdn_cli and gdn_tauri_check) and the desktop shell's own Rust source
under src-tauri/, are under the MIT License. Each crate carries the licence as its own
LICENSE file, and the text is below.

The page under page-source/ is built from parts, and each part says at its top which
licence it carries. Most are MIT. Seven (06_mge.js, 26_water.js, 29_ssao.js, 33_fxaa.js,
35_underwater.js, 36_dof.js, 37_shadow.js) are under the GNU General Public License,
version 2, because they carry code ported from MGE XE, which is GPL-2.0. The built page
(Gardenfell.html, ui/index.html) contains all of them and is distributed under the
GPL-2.0 as a whole; an MIT part taken on its own stays MIT. The texts and the list are in
page-source/LICENSE. The desktop application as installed carries the page, and so it is
distributed under the GPL-2.0 as a whole; a program that uses only the crates, or only
the page's MIT parts, is bound by the MIT terms alone.

NOTICE, beside this file, names every piece that came from elsewhere or was written to
match another program's behaviour.

